course: dictionary
lesson: 7513
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word pound is one of them. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it, which is the context. The context gives the clues.
explain: «Theo's grandma sent twenty pounds in cash.» Twenty and cash are clues about money, so here pound means money. A pound (£) is the money of the United Kingdom.
explain: A loaf of bread weighs about one pound, so here pound is a unit of weight. Words like flour, sugar and fruit are clues that a weight is meant. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Pound can also be a verb, an action word. To pound is to hit hard again and again. This is why a heart can be pounding when it beats very fast and hard.
fact: Pound is a noun or a verb, depending on how it is used in the sentence.
fact: A pound (£) is the money of the United Kingdom, and a pound has 100 pence.
fact: A pound is also a unit of weight: one pound is 16 ounces, written lb.
fact: To pound means to hit hard again and again.
fact: A pound can also be a place where lost dogs or towed cars are kept.
exercise: «Harry also took a pound from Mum's purse for a lolly.» In this sentence, what is a pound? | To hit hard | A unit of weight | A place where lost dogs are kept | *Money
exercise: A loaf of bread weighs about one pound. What does pound mean here? | To hit hard again and again | Money | A place for towed cars | *A unit of weight
exercise: The waves pounded the rocks all night. What does pounded mean? | A unit of weight | Money paid for a drink | *To hit hard again and again | A place where lost things are kept
test: «The dog was taken to the pound after it ran off.» What does pound mean in this sentence? | *A place where lost dogs are kept | A unit of weight | To hit hard again and again | Money
test: «Theo's grandma sent twenty pounds in cash.» Which clue shows that pound means money? | Sent | *Twenty and cash | It is a long sentence | Grandma
exam: Which meaning of pound fits best in «The bag of sugar weighed two pounds»? | Money | To hit hard | A place where bags are kept | *A unit of weight
